From d25b5d5a5e18cbf2d76ace82b80089b571c32838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:46:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [Test] PLE BF16->FP8 conversion: quantiser and
 loader-contract tests

Covers the converter that turns the Flash-Next BF16 PLE n-gram table
(ple-bf16-*.safetensors) into the FP8 E4M3 form ple_layer.py's FP8 path
expects.

Contract assertions are taken from the real code, not restated:
Qwen4ExpPLEFp8EmbeddingMethod.create_weights supplies the required
parameter names/dtypes/shapes, Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.load_weights
supplies the "ngram_embedding.shard_" and "ngram_embedding.weight_scale"
literals, Qwen4ExpPLELayer._dequantize_embeddings pins the scale as
multiplicative, and serve.sh supplies the detection glob the output
filenames must satisfy.

TP rank/size are stubbed rather than initialising NCCL so the tests run
on CPU without touching a GPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
